Mood/Vibe: Sterile, ancient, yet deeply organic—the feeling of a garden growing in a machine.

Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Telescope Lens eats a Sunbeam
- Story & Context: While peering through a warped rooftop lens, Silas watched the vault ventilation system flicker and accidentally broadcast the archives’ first melody into the atmosphere. The smell of burning ozone hit his nostrils as the song rippled through the city power grid, and he whispered to his companion, "we’ve opened the cellar door to the stars." The track is a frantic, shimmering surge of metallic rhythm that captures the moment the vault’s silence was finally broken.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A cracked telescope lens reflecting a vibrant, distorted sunset, macro photography, high contrast, golden hour glow melting into icy blue deep shadows.

Track 2: Yalla-klimat
- Story & Context: Muna hides in the storage unit, confessing her love for the dormant wheat strands while the guards hunt for the source of the forbidden, melodic vibrations. She holds a handful of cracked soil, realizing the seeds are actually singing back in a language she never learned, feeling the cold air cling to her skin. She hums the hook, "my pulse is a language buried in grain," as she realizes there is no way to return to the world above.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a human hand holding ancient dried seeds, neon-tinted steam rising, a dark industrial room, cinematic lighting, grain and grit textures.

Track 3: The North Star is off by a Degree
- Story & Context: Years after the vault collapse, legend says the inhabitants turned into static energy, leaving behind a garden that glows in the dark of the permanent winter. Residents of the city look up and realize the stars have shifted slightly, believing it is the archive finally ascending into the night sky, leaving a scent of jasmine in the sub-zero air. The music fades into a distant, metallic chant as the myth of the "Singing Seed-Keepers" becomes the only remaining truth, with the chorus echoing, "gravity bends where the archive ends."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An ink-black sky with geometric patterns formed by constellations, glowing bioluminescent flowers sprouting from metallic pipes in the foreground, dreamlike and surreal.

